{"name":"Half Moon","hex":"#cccdb9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"half moon","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of half-moon."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/half_moon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lunar phase","blocks":[{"text":"A lunar phase or Moon phase is the apparent shape of the Moon's day and night phases of the lunar day as viewed from afar. Because the Moon is tidally locked to Earth, the cycle of phases takes one lunar month and moves across the same side of the Moon, which always faces Earth. In common usage, the four major phases are the new moon, the first quarter, the full moon, and the last quarter. The four minor phases are waxing crescent, waxing gibbous, waning gibbous, and waning crescent. A lunar month is the time between successive recurrences of the same phase: due to the eccentricity of the Moon's orbit, this duration is not perfectly constant but averages about 29.5 days."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Moon_Phase_Diagram_for_Simple_English_Wikipedia.GIF/330px-Moon_Phase_Diagram_for_Simple_English_Wikipedia.GIF?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lunar_phase","wikidata":"Q26388"},{"title":"Semicircle","blocks":[{"text":"In mathematics, a semicircle is a one-dimensional locus of points that forms half of a circle. It is a circular arc that measures 180°. It only has one line of symmetry."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Semicircle-curve.svg/330px-Semicircle-curve.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Semicircle","wikidata":"Q1133242"},{"title":"Half Moon (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Half Moon is a 2006 internationally co-produced Kurdish comedy-drama film directed by Bahman Ghobadi, who co-wrote the screenplay with Behnam Behzadi, partly inspired by Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart's Requiem. The film stars Ismail Ghaffari as Mamo, an old legendary musician, who sets to trespass the borders of Iranian Kurdistan to give one final concert in Iraqi Kurdistan with his 10 sons."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/51/Half_Moon_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Half_Moon_(film)","wikidata":"Q701124"},{"title":"One half","blocks":[{"text":"One half is the multiplicative inverse of 2. It is an irreducible fraction with a numerator of 1 and a denominator of 2. It often appears in mathematical equations, recipes and measurements."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/One_half","wikidata":"Q2114394"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Moondrop.jpg/500px-Moondrop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Moondrop.jpg/500px-Moondrop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A full moon sets behind San Gorgonio Mountain in California on a midsummer's morning.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMoondrop.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Moon_phases_en.jpg/500px-Moon_phases_en.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Moon_phases_en.jpg/1280px-Moon_phases_en.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Moon_phases_en.jpg/500px-Moon_phases_en.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The phases of the Moon as viewed looking southward from the Northern Hemisphere. Each phase would be rotated 180° if seen looking northward from the Southern Hemisphere. The upper part of the diagram is not to scale, as the Moon, the  Earth, and the Moon's orbit are all much smaller relative to the Earth's orbit than shown here.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMoon_phases_en.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/New_Moon.jpg/500px-New_Moon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/New_Moon.jpg/1280px-New_Moon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/New_Moon.jpg/500px-New_Moon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANew_Moon.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Waxing_crescent_moon%2C_October_28%2C_2025._Taken_with_with_a_Nikon_Z6II_camera_and_Sigma_150-600mm_f_5-6.3_DG_OS_HSM_lens.jpg/500px-Waxing_crescent_moon%2C_October_28%2C_2025._Taken_with_with_a_Nikon_Z6II_camera_and_Sigma_150-600mm_f_5-6.3_DG_OS_HSM_lens.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Waxing_crescent_moon%2C_October_28%2C_2025._Taken_with_with_a_Nikon_Z6II_camera_and_Sigma_150-600mm_f_5-6.3_DG_OS_HSM_lens.jpg/500px-Waxing_crescent_moon%2C_October_28%2C_2025._Taken_with_with_a_Nikon_Z6II_camera_and_Sigma_150-600mm_f_5-6.3_DG_OS_HSM_lens.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWaxing_crescent_moon%2C_October_28%2C_2025._Taken_with_with_a_Nikon_Z6II_camera_and_Sigma_150-600mm_f_5-6.3_DG_OS_HSM_lens.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Daniel_Hershman_-_march_moon_%28by%29.jpg/500px-Daniel_Hershman_-_march_moon_%28by%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thu